## Notebooks

`ipykernel` is a dev dependency, so after `make setup` you can pick the
project's `.venv` as the kernel in VS Code or Jupyter. The package is installed
in editable mode, so `from {{ package_name }} import ...` works in notebooks.

On commit, [nbstripout](https://github.com/kynan/nbstripout) strips outputs and
execution counts, and ruff lints and formats notebook cells.

## Pre-commit hooks

- **Basic hygiene:** trailing whitespace, end-of-file newline, YAML/TOML syntax,
  large files, merge conflict markers, private keys
- **ruff:** lint (with auto-fix) and format
- **nbstripout:** strip notebook outputs
- **uv-lock:** keep `uv.lock` in sync with `pyproject.toml`

